{"id": "EUVD-2026-103510", "enisaUuid": "23e0a1fd-c6b6-3339-9360-42e3d58ed64e", "description": "libspatialite through 5.1.0 fails to validate the polygon ring count in ParseWkbPolygon, allowing attackers to trigger uncontrolled interior-ring allocation via crafted geometry BLOBs. Attackers can supply a crafted polygon in a SpatiaLite database or ST_GeomFromWKB input to crash the process or corrupt heap memory on 32-bit builds.", "datePublished": "2026-10-18T12:19:36", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-20T15:31:53", "baseScore": 6.9, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:L/AC:L/AT:N/PR:N/UI:P/VC:N/VI:L/VA:H/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://hackmd.io/@haindpwn/libspatialite-wkb-geometry-count-overflow", "https://www.gaia-gis.it/fossil/libspatialite/file?name=src/gaiageo/gg_wkb.c&ci=5a5528e8d2", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/libspatialite-through-5.1.0-uncontrolled-memory-allocation-via-parsewkbpolygon-ring-count"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-112048", "GHSA-w35v-6xgp-6m6w"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.12, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "3a39b354-9314-3dc0-8c9d-742440e2abce", "product": {"name": "libspatialite", "vendor": {"name": "SpatiaLite"}}, "product_version": "0 \u22645.1.0"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "ec583d18-958b-3173-b02e-3406ffe44c80", "vendor": {"name": "SpatiaLite"}}], "isExploited": false}